# E551 — Route in-dialog SUBSCRIBE refreshes to the existing NTA dialog
id:                     E3600
trigger_tool:           test|runtime
phase:                  testing
error_signature:        re.?SUBSCRIBE|nua_i_subscribe.*(timeout|500|100.*200)|test_subscribe_notify\(\).*100.*200|SUBSCRIBE.*(new handle|default leg)
severity:               2
category:               compat, portability, network
match_keywords:         Sofia-SIP, NTA, NUA, SUBSCRIBE refresh, dialog routing
title:                  Route in-dialog SUBSCRIBE and unsubscribe requests to the existing NTA dialog
root_cause:             NTA excluded sip_method_subscribe from its existing-leg lookup, so tagged refresh and Expires: 0 requests missed the established dialog. The regression callback must answer each request. Its saved nua_i_subscribe event is a request notification with status 100; the client-side nua_r_unsubscribe event carries the final SIP 200.
affected_scope:         Sofia-SIP NTA/NUA event subscriptions that refresh within an established SIP dialog; test callbacks that observe refreshes must explicitly respond.
verification_cmd:       On HarmonyOS AArch64 run finish sofia-sip 1.13.18 built. Confirm NUA-11.4.3 refresh and NUA-11.4.4 unsubscribe; expect the server nua_i_subscribe request event status 100 and client nua_r_unsubscribe final SIP status 200. Confirm all individual check_sofia items and Conan test_package consumer plus GLib/loopback SIP test pass.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:            route-subscribe-refresh-by-dialog
rec_description:        Allow tagged in-dialog SUBSCRIBE and Expires: 0 requests to use the existing NTA leg lookup. The regression callback explicitly answers refresh and unsubscribe requests before waiting for NOTIFY; assert NUA event status 100 separately from client SIP response 200.
rec_command:             In nta.c, remove the sip_method_subscribe exclusion from leg_find() when resolving an existing dialog; in test_simple.c answer refresh/unsubscribe using NUTAG_WITH(nua_current_request(nua)) and Expires 365/0, expect nua_i_subscribe status 100 and nua_r_unsubscribe final status 200.
rec_auto_fix:            false
rec_impl:                0026-libsofia-sip-ua-nta-nta.c.patch
fallback_priority:       2
fallback_approach:       preserve-refresh-on-original-nua-handle
fallback_description:    If dialog lookup cannot safely identify the established leg, update the existing notifier usage on its original NUA handle without creating a second handle.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:       false
fallback_impl:
forbid_1_pattern:        method\s*!=\s*sip_method_subscribe|auto.?200.*SUBSCRIBE.*runtime
forbid_1_reason:         Excluding in-dialog SUBSCRIBE prevents dialog refresh routing; automatically answering in the library bypasses the application callback contract.
forbid_1_consequence:    Refreshes create a new NUA handle instead of updating the established notifier dialog, or silently accept requests that the application has not handled.
principles:
doc_file:               doc/E551.md
last_updated: 2026-10-18
source_event:           Sofia-SIP 1.13.18 HarmonyOS AArch64 W3: NUA-11.4.3 tagged refresh and NUA-11.4.4 unsubscribe both pass; the server nua_i_subscribe event reports 100 while the client receives final SIP 200, and all 8 check_sofia Check cases pass.
authors:
source_pr:
source_commit:
metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     1.0
metrics_last_used:      2026-10-18
authors:               8F61
